WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.160
In the UK, the label on a
wall socket says 230 volts.

2
00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:07.490
But the voltage is never steady.

3
00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:11.460
It follows a sine curve,
alternating at 50 hertz.

4
00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:17.700
At every crest it reaches 325 volts,
well above the number on the label.

5
00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:21.340
An oscilloscope can draw that
wave on a grid of squares.

6
00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:25.040
How do you read its size and
frequency off the screen?

7
00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:28.100
In this mission, you'll
name the parts of a wave:

8
00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:32.320
its peak, its peak-to-peak
value and its period.

9
00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:36.890
Then you'll find out what the
230 on the label really measures.

10
00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:42.110
Your mission: work out how to read a
wave's size and frequency off the screen.
